<title>UK: Eurotunnel job cuts face court threat-report.</title>
<headline>Eurotunnel job cuts face court threat-report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eurotunnel Plc, the Anglo-French Channel Tunnel operator struggling under 9.1 billion stg in debt, may face a union attempt to block its plans to axe 657 jobs, said a report in The Times on Monday.</p>
<p>The report said five French unions are set to call in an external accountant to review Eurotunnel accounts and come up with alternative cost cutting measures - a move which could then lead to a court challenge.</p>
<p>The UK-based Transport and General Workers Union has also rejected the cuts and plans a campaign against the job losses.</p>
<p>Eurotunnel has estimated that the job cuts will reduce its salary bill by 16 million stg this year.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
